ones at G8 and H9. The most strategic approach for Black is to seize the initiative by extending their own active line rather than playing defensively. Extending the diagonal G9-H8 to I7 creates an "Open 3" (a line of three stones with open ends). This is a forcing move (sente) because White must immediately block to prevent Black from forming an "Open 4" on the next turn, which would lead to an unstoppable win. This move allows Black to dictate the flow of the game.\n\nReason: The move creates a diagonal Open 3 (G9-H8-I7). This is the strongest immediate threat available, forcing the opponent to defend and allowing Black to keep the initiative.\n\nAnswer: {"col": "I", "row": 7}'}
